WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.470 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  video game fans have plenty of questions  about the movie adaptation of uncharted  for one did tom holland really pull off  the role of nathan drake even after  seeing the film some questions will  linger keep watching for the biggest  after being caught breaking and entering  and threatened with prison nate's  brother sam escapes from the orphanage  where the brothers live sam promises  he'll come back but he never does  leaving nate to wonder where sam went  nate's mentor victor sully sullivan  admits that sam used to be his treasure  hunting partner yet he avoids talking  about sam's fate for most of the film i  think you're here because you're your  brother well you know my brother said  eventually it becomes clear that sully  and his sometimes ally chloe believes  sam is dead the mercenary braddock even  indicates she's the one who killed him  at the end of the film though there's a  brief scene set in a dingy prison that  indicates sam is still kicking we see a  man writing a postcard the form of  communication he used to reach out to  nate but where is he and how did he  survive as sully chloe and braddock all  thought they saw him die there are  several tantalizing ways that nate and  sully could learn about sam's situation  they could find out from a third party  and rescue him nate could find out sully  secretly knows the truth about sam  leading to a rift or sam could escape  and seek out the pair in some unexpected  way there's plenty of fodder for a  sequel  uncharted makes it seem as though  santiago mankata is the film's main  villain but when braddock the mercenary  he hired kills him midway through the  film she becomes the true antagonist  mankato was willing to do whatever it  took to find and claim magellan's  treasure but he didn't like to get his  hands dirty braddock on the other hand  is more than happy to get her hands  dirty and has a band of goons who seem  to share her cutthroat impulses that  doesn't mean she's a great villain her  motivations mostly seem to revolve  around the desire for a massive payday  still she keeps the film's fight scenes  interesting including the final fight on  one of magellan's ships when she loses  the fight and falls into the ocean that  ship ends up crashing into the water on  top of her given the circumstances it  seems like braddock must have died on  contact but there are plenty of movies  that have made it seem like the villain  is dead only to resurrect them in the  sequel if say braddock was a strong  swimmer she could have gotten away  before the ship hit the sea and we  wouldn't have seen it  the movie's mid-credits sequence sets up  nate and sully's next adventure nate  meets a man with an eye patch to make a  trade to acquire a map that will lead to  nazi treasure although it's never clear  what specifically he's hoping to find in  world war ii the nazis confiscated and  looted all kinds of valuable art and  artifacts so it wouldn't be all that  surprising if nate and sully decided to  go after one of those treasures besides  nazis come up a couple of times during  the uncharted game so it's possible  their mention in the mid credits scene  is an indication that although this  uncharted film told an original story  the plot of the sequel will take its  cues from the plot of one of the games  either way going up against nazis is a  popular trope in action adventure films  everyone from indiana jones to captain  america have done it so perhaps it's no  surprise that nathan drake and sully  would do so as well  the man that nate meets in the  mid-credits scene references his boss  during their exchange we don't know much  about this boss but one of the things he  requests in exchange for the nazi map is  the ring nate wears on a strap around  his neck the ring has sentimental value  for nate it was originally sam's and sam  gave it to nate when he left yet as nate  points out it has no real world value  the man with the eyepatch's boss isn't  seeking financial gain though his boss  wants it because it has value to nate it  seems as though this unseen boss could  be an interesting antagonist of course  it's unclear whether he will be the main  villain in the next movie as nate and  sully could find themselves racing  against someone else to claim the  treasure yet the fact that this boss is  still unknown indicates he could be a  big player in the next film could this  be a villain from the uncharted games or  maybe it's sam himself after all if sam  escaped from prison and amassed his own  gang it could explain why the man with  the eye patch said his boss wanted  nate's ring  in the last moments in the mid-credits  scene sully shows up to help nate when  the meeting with the man with the eye  patch goes south after sully gets the  situation under control nate and sully  leap together they bicker about sully's  delayed arrival until they see something  that stops them in their tracks the  final second of the film shows them  looking dumbfounded but what do they see  it's entirely possible that they run  into a new character or characters that  we won't meet until the sequel or they  may have encountered a character we're  familiar with perhaps braddock is really  alive and has finally hunted them down  or perhaps this is the point where sam  reveals he's still among the living  there are a ton of possibilities but  without an idea of the potential story  for the sequel it's hard to narrow them  down what else aren't you telling me  sully summons chloe frazier when he and  nate first arrive in spain even though  chloe initially antagonizes them they  eventually team up to track down a map  to help them find magellan's gold nate  and sully quickly learned she wasn't  entirely trustworthy she was actually  working for mankata and she regularly  makes it clear that she doesn't trust  anyone even so she eventually helps them  reclaim the artifacts they need from  mankato's plane by the time nate figures  out the location of the treasure he  knows he can't trust chloe so he leaves  a set of fake coordinates just in case  she takes off before he wakes up  unfortunately for chloe she takes the  bait which means instead of finding the  gold with him she goes on a wild goose  chase  the movie gives no indication of what  that means for her relationship with  nate or sully leaving open the question  of what could happen if she ever meets  up with them again  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stuff are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

